          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "qahr kardan pairs qahr, borrowed from Arabic qahr, \"force, wrath\" (root q-h-r, Lane), with the Persian verb kardan, \"to do, to make\". kardan, \"to do\", is an inherited verb, from Middle Persian kardan (EtymDB). Persian uses it for sulking and refusing to speak."
            }
